On 6/17/07, m.kornig@sondal.net <m.kornig@sondal.net> wrote:
>
> Interesting. This is probably convient for an experienced
> reader/speaker, in particular for a group of smaller words
> that often apear together.


Words in a form of set rather than being separated may also benefit the
beginners as it helps grasp/memorise phrases quicker: {puziku mi gunka}
rather than {pu zi ku mi gunka}, {mi bazaze'avu gunka} rather than {mi ba za
ze'a vu gunka}. This way the sentence structure (or the grammatical blocks)
becomes clearer (though it is always unambiguous) & beginner-friendly.

Vid

